{"id": "4011130e-b565-419b-9f52-64c5491e5579", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "The error text and missing Lambda logs are themselves diagnostic (no invocation ever reached the function, so logs wouldn't exist) — this points at the resource-policy hop. I'll run the full authorization-chain trace against your account now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_mJCo5JSmccvBbTuGii2fl5", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"deep_research": true, "prompt": "{
  "task": "Diagnose a DependencyFailedException access-denial on an Amazon Lex V2 bot invoking a Lambda fulfillment function. Use the aiml-access-diagnostics skill methodology end to end (read it via skill_read first, then follow its checklist: classify, establish identity/scope, collect evidence via policy reads first, walk the six-hop authorization chain, apply Lex-specific knowledge from references/svc-lex.md, assign verdicts, propose a scoped policy, and render the full report per references/report-format.md).",
  "context": "User reports Lex conversation fails with: 'DependencyFailedException: Invalid Bot Configuration: Access denied while invoking lambda function [redacted ARN] from [redacted ARN]. Please check the policy on this function.' The Lambda function has NO CloudWatch log entries for the failed invocation attempts -- this suggests the call never reached inside the function, consistent with a resource-policy (Lambda-based policy / lex:InvokeFunction permission) denial rather than an in-function failure. Likely root cause is the Lambda resource policy (function policy) missing a statement granting lex.amazonaws.com permission to invoke this function with a SourceArn matching this specific bot alias, OR the existing statement's SourceArn/SourceAccount condition not matching this bot-alias ARN. Follow the skill's Lex-specific guidance (svc-lex.md) on Mode 3 Lambda code-hook authorization, the runtime bot-alias ARN format, and non-denial causes to rule out.",
  "resources": [
    "[redacted ARN]",
    "[redacted ARN]",
    "account 012345678901_1",
    "region us-east-1"
  ],
  "timeframe": "recent / at time of reported failure (Lambda has no logs, so timeframe cannot be narrowed via log timestamps -- rely on CloudTrail if available and current resource-policy/IAM state)",
  "criteria": "Walk all six authorization-chain hops (caller/IAM, iam:PassRole where applicable, Lex service role, Lambda resource-based policy / lex:InvokeFunction, Lambda execution role if reachable, SCP). Name the specific denying hop with evidence (e.g. missing or mismatched Lambda resource policy statement). Rule out non-denial causes (unbuilt locale, disabled code hook, region mismatch). Produce the proposed scoped policy/resource-policy statement for human review. Follow the skill's output discipline -- full report format, no narration of each API call."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Diagnose Lex-to-Lambda access denial via IAM/resource-policy chain in account 012345678901_1."}], "created_at": null}
